      <Placemark><name>Bluestone Travel Plaza</name><styleUrl>#public</styleUrl><description>NB MM 17.22 (signed MP 18). Public - state (Parkways Authority) | Access: NB only | Spaces: Public - WVDOT Rest Areas GIS layer: 70 (before the 2025 rebuild); WV Parkways Authority (as reported in trade press): 79 (69 pre-rebuild + 10 added); Study corridor sketch (data.png): 117 | Private - TruckStopsAndServices.com (TSS): 65 | Satellite count (Esri World Imagery dated 2025-10-22): 35 spots counted along parking rows (14 occupied, 21 empty on the image) | Sources differ: 35 to 117 | Status: Open (rebuilt; reopened mid-Jan 2025) | Cost: Free; no reservations | Restrooms: Yes | Showers: No | 24/7 staff: Yes (24/7 Mountain State Market) | Lighting: Yes (24/7 facility) | New building; Wendy's; EV chargers in development; pet relief; picnic; imagery (post-rebuild era): new building/canopy/fresh concrete confirmed; ~4 angled truck rows visible with 14-18 trucks; east rows cloud-obscured so full 79 not countable</description><Point><coordinates>-81.0677,37.4748,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
      <Placemark><name>Camp Creek Wayside (I-77 SB MM 18 parking area)</name><styleUrl>#public</styleUrl><description>SB MM 18.3. Public - state (Parkways) | Access: SB only (field-verified) | Spaces: Public - Study team field count: 12; WVDOT Rest Areas GIS layer: 13 | Private - TruckStopsAndServices.com (TSS): listed; no parking count published | Satellite count (Esri World Imagery dated 2025-10-22): 7 spots counted along parking rows (6 occupied, 1 empty on the image) | Sources differ: 7 to 13 | Status: Open | Cost: Free | Restrooms: No (no facilities - field-verified) | Showers: No | 24/7 staff: No | Lighting: Unknown | Parking-only teardrop wayside across turnpike from Bluestone; no buildings; long accel/decel lanes; 5 tractor-trailers visible in imagery</description><Point><coordinates>-81.0802,37.4858,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
